<Defs>

  <!--
    The plans of release D's peoples' towns (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release D"; the format is in Rimfolk_TownPlans.xml's
    header; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeopleTowns.cs places them). Only the base game's buildings, so every plan stands
    without the DLCs; the tests check every plan (Tools/Tests/PeoplesTests.cs). Each tells its people's story: the
    Wardens' lodge behind its palisade with a lantern post on every road out, the Quiet Bell's walled grave-garden, the
    Circuit's bout-rings and stables, and the Wheel's yard inside a ring of its carts, laid out as if leaving tomorrow.
  -->

  <ColonyCouncil.TownPlanDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Plan_WardensLodge</defName>
    <label>wardens' lodge</label>
    <description>The Lantern Wardens' lodge: a palisade of logs with a gate on the north road and the south, a lantern post either side of each, the lodge of bunks, the trophy hall of long tables between posts hung with what was hunted, a yard with a fire, a butcher's spot and a hide-scraper's, the kennels for the hounds, and the storehouse.</description>
